.TH "SCLIP" "1" "January 2020" "secure-terminal" "secure-terminal Manual"
.SH "NAME"
\fBsclip\fR \- sanitize clipboard\-bound text to safe characters
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBsclip\fR [\fB\-\-unicode\fR] [\fB\-\-summary\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
sclip reads text on standard input and writes clipboard\-safe text on standard output\. It is a pure filter \-\- it opens no files, needs no display and never touches the clipboard itself \-\- so it composes with the system clipboard tools and confines tightly under AppArmor:
.IP "" 4
.nf
wl\-paste | sclip | wl\-copy
xclip \-o | sclip | xclip \-i
.fi
.IP "" 0
.P
The purpose is to make text safe to paste into an editor, or any program that does not neutralize Unicode: invisible, zero\-width, bidirectional\-control and other control characters are removed\.
.P
By default sclip is STRICTEST: it keeps only printable ASCII plus tab and newline, so a cross\-script homoglyph (a look\-alike posing as ASCII) cannot ride out either\.
.P
The \fBst\-wl\-paste\fR(1), \fBst\-wl\-copy\fR(1) and \fBst\-xclip\fR(1) drop\-in wrappers run these pipelines for you\.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-unicode\fR
Keep printable non\-ASCII characters (accents, CJK, \|\.\|\.\|\.) instead of dropping them\. Note the honest limit: a homoglyph IS printable Unicode, so \fB\-\-unicode\fR does NOT remove look\-alikes; it removes only the invisible, bidirectional and control classes\. Use the default, or the review GUI (\fBsecure\-terminal \-\-clipboard\-watch\fR), when look\-alikes matter\.
.TP
\fB\-\-summary\fR
Write a one\-line, mode\-accurate report of what was removed (and, in \fB\-\-unicode\fR mode, what printable non\-ASCII was kept) to standard error\. Standard output is unchanged\.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success; 1 on an unreadable input or a closed output pipe; 2 on an unknown option\.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBst\-wl\-paste\fR(1), \fBst\-wl\-copy\fR(1), \fBst\-xclip\fR(1), \fBsecure\-terminal\fR(1), \fBunicode\-tag\fR(1)
